    {
      "note": "The ASV recasts מִיּוֹם, from the day, as the duration expression so long, bounded by unto this day later in the clause. Neither so nor long has a clearly preferable independent allocation between מִן and יוֹם, so this residual phrase remains noncompositional under rules 2 and 6. The source head is יוֹם, carrying the temporal content, and the English anchor is long; rule 23 gives the content morpheme priority over the opening preposition, and rule 40 expressly extends the noun-headed temporal-adverb analysis to an absolute noun. Heading on מִן by the first-token fallback is the competing reading, but rule 6 requires the lexical-head rules to be considered before that fallback. The written אֲשֶׁר separately takes as, whose subordinating force is independently recoverable under rules 11 and 30; this corrects the chapter convention's whole-fusion premise.",
      "source": [
        "s015",
        "s016"
      ],
      "source_head": "s016",
      "status": "noncompositional",
      "target": [
        "t019",
        "t020"
      ],
      "target_head": "t020"
    },
    {
